# Dabuj environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env` if you use a tool that loads one. Dabuj itself reads these
# directly from the environment; it does not require a .env file.
#
# Normal configuration lives in `dabuj.toml` in your data directory
# (`dabuj system-info` prints the path). These variables exist for cases that
# must be settable before the configuration file is read.

# Relocate the entire application data directory: models, projects, cache, logs
# and the config file. Useful for portable installs and for testing.
# DABUJ_DATA_DIR=/path/to/dabuj-data

# --- Not used, and deliberately so -------------------------------------------
#
# Dabuj has no API keys, no licence keys, no telemetry endpoint and no update
# server. There are no secrets to configure because there is nothing to
# authenticate against.
#
# If optional cloud providers are ever added, their credentials will be read
# from the environment (never stored in the config file or in a project), and
# they will only be usable with `privacy.allow_cloud_providers` explicitly
# turned on. See docs/PRIVACY.md.
